  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor with plate area &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&#39; and distance of separation &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&#39; is filled with a dielectric. What is the capacity of the capacitor when permittivity of the dielectric varies as:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></math>, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
